Error [jet.FailureDomainNotErrorType]: `impl Celsius -> Float` converts failures into `Float`, which is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/error_conversions/value_target_is_not_an_error_type.jet:8:17
    |
  8 | impl Celsius -> Float {
    |                 ^^^^^
 Why: `impl Source -> Target` is a failure conversion: it applies when a `Source` failure propagates where a `Target` failure is expected, and a value type such as `Float` describes no failure.
 Fix: To turn a `Celsius` value into a `Float`, write a function that takes `Celsius` and returns `Float`; to convert failures, name `Err`, a Core error or an `#Error` type as the target.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417
